LM Studio is another tool for running AI language models locally on your laptop. Think of it as a desktop application where you can download a model, chat with it, and run a local API without needing to write Python code first.
Run models locally using a graphical interface (GUI), with an API option too.
Step 1 — Install ,Download it from the official 
Step 2 — Download a model-Open Discover, search for a small model, and download a suitable version. This uses laptop storage. 
Step 3 — Open the Chat tab, load your downloaded model, and ask a question. You don't need Python or terminal commands for basic chatting.
>>Preset:-is a saved collection of settings that controls how the model generates its answers.Think of it as a ready-made configuration that you can reuse.
   Temperature: Controls randomness.
   Top-K / Top-P: Controls which candidate tokens can be selected.
   System prompt: Instructions about how the model should behave, if included in that preset.
   Other generation settings supported by the application.
